<title>UK: List of Britain's new Labour cabinet.</title>
<headline>List of Britain's new Labour cabinet.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's new Labour Prime Minister Tony Blair, swept to victory in an election landslide on Thursday, has appointed his cabinet, fulfilling his pledge to &quot;hit the ground running&quot; after taking power.</p>
<p>The following is a list of the members of his cabinet:</p>
<p> Prime Minister.................................Tony Blair</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister..........................John Prescott</p>
<p> Chancellor of the Exchequer....................Gordon Brown</p>
<p> Foreign and Commonwealth Secretary.. ..........Robin Cook</p>
<p> Lord Chancellor................................Lord Irvine</p>
<p> Home Secretary.................................Jack Straw</p>
<p> Education and Employment Secretary.............David Blunkett</p>
<p> Trade and Industry Secretary...................Margaret Beckett</p>
<p> Transport Secretary............................Gavin Strang</p>
<p> Social Security Secretary......................Harriet Harman</p>
<p> Defence Secretary..............................George Robertson</p>
<p> Health Secretary...............................Frank Dobson</p>
<p> Leader of the House of Commons.................Ann Taylor</p>
<p> Agriculture Secretary..........................Jack Cunningham</p>
<p> Heritage Secretary.............................Chris Smith</p>
<p> Northern Ireland Secretary.....................Marjorie Mowlam</p>
<p> Scottish Secretary.............................Donald Dewar</p>
<p> Welsh Secretary................................Ron Davies</p>
<p> International Development Secretary............Clare Short</p>
<p> Chief Secretary to the Treasury................Alistair Darling</p>
<p> Chancellor of the Duchy of Lancaster...........David Clark</p>
<p> Leader of the House of Lords...................Lord Richard</p>
<p>    ................</p>
<p>Non-cabinet appointments</p>
<p> Chief Whip.....................................Nick Brown</p>
<p> Minister of state for Social Security..........Frank Field</p>
<p> Minister of State for Employment...............Andrew Smith</p>
</text>
